y &= \tan x + \cot x \\
&= \frac{\sin x}{\cos x} + \frac{\cos x}{\sin x} \\
&= \frac{\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x}{\sin x \cos x} \\
&= \frac{1}{\sin x \cos x} \\
&= \frac{2}{2 \sin x \cos x} \\
&= \frac{2}{\sin 2x}
\end{align*}
Therefore, the period of $y$ is $\boxed{\pi}$.The period of the tangent and cotangent functions is $\pi$, so the period of $y = \tan x + \cot x$ is also $\pi$.

